   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the correction law, in relation to the correctional\nassociation's ability to access, visit, inspect, and examine all state\ncorrectional facilities; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2020 amending\nthe correction law relating to permitting the correctional association to\naccess, visit, inspect, and examine all state correctional facilities, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 8046 and A. 10194, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S875",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S875-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §146, Cor L; amd §3, Chap of 2020 (as proposed in S.8046 & A.10194)",
    "lawSection": "Correction Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S875\n\nSPONSOR: SEPULVEDA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the correction law, in relation to the correctional\nassociation's ability to access, visit, inspect, and examine all state\ncorrectional facilities; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2020\namending the correction law relating to permitting the correctional\nassociation to access, visit, inspect, and examine all state correction-\nal facilities, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 8046 and A.\n10194, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2020,\nc.320.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by limiting CANY's access\nto correctional facilities by increasing notice requirements and limit-\ning CANY's access to certain records.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Executive expressed concerns over the broad grant of authority to\nCANY and DOCCS's ability to accommodate such visits without certain\nlimitations. This legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying\nchapter that addresses those concerns.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 320 of the Laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis bill would have no fiscal impact on the State or localities. This\nbill is regulatory and requires no additional resources to execute.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
